[TITLE]
Demand categories fixture (ROADMAP Task 468). AUTHORED HERE, not an EPA file.
Net1, Net2 and Net3 all have an EMPTY [DEMANDS] section, so none of them exercises a
demand category at all -- which is why the importer's flattening went untested for so
long. This is the smallest network that does exercise one, and every row of [DEMANDS]
below is here to make one statement the [JUNCTIONS] column cannot make:
  J1  three categories, two patterns, and a third row with a category and NO pattern
  J2  one category, one pattern -- itemized even though the column could have held it
  J3  one category and no pattern
  J4  no [DEMANDS] row at all: the ordinary junction, which must not change
  J5  a [JUNCTIONS] demand AND [DEMANDS] rows, the case where EPANET DISCARDS the column
The number TEXTS are deliberately not what String(parseFloat(x)) returns -- 50.0, 12.50,
0.750 -- so a writer that formats rather than remembering is caught.

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID              	Elev        	Demand      	Pattern
 J1              	100
 J2              	95
 J3              	90.5
 J4              	88          	33.0        	Pat2
 J5              	86          	100

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID              	Head        	Pattern
 R1              	200

[PIPES]
;ID              	Node1           	Node2           	Length      	Diameter    	Roughness   	MinorLoss   	Status
 P1              	R1              	J1              	1000        	12          	130         	0           	Open
 P2              	J1              	J2              	800         	10          	130         	0           	Open
 P3              	J2              	J3              	800         	8           	130         	0           	Open
 P4              	J3              	J4              	600         	8           	130         	0           	Open
 P5              	J4              	J5              	600         	8           	130         	0           	Open
 P6              	J5              	J1              	1200        	8           	130         	0           	Open

[DEMANDS]
;Junction        	Demand      	Pattern         	Category
 J1              	50.0        	Pat1            	;Elm Acres
 J1              	20          	Pat2            	;Elm Acres Park
 J1              	12.50       	                	;Taco Bell 354
 J2              	18          	Pat1            	;Rio Vista Apartments
 J3              	7.5         	                	;Mesa Elementary School
 J5              	40          	Pat1            	;Sunset Estates
 J5              	0.750       	Pat2            	;Sunset Estates common area

[PATTERNS]
;ID              	Multipliers
 Pat1            	0.6         	1.0         	1.4         	1.0
 Pat2            	0.2         	0.5         	2.3         	1.0

[TIMES]
 Duration        	24:00
 Hydraulic Timestep	1:00
